<!-- Buying guide (unique local copy; facts from this page, manufacturer spec pages, and /guides/) -->
<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <h2>Who South Seas Spas are for</h2>
        <p>South Seas is the line we point people to when they want lots of choice at an accessible price. With more than fifteen models across the Deluxe and Standard classes, you can choose loungers or benches, compact or family-size, and different jet layouts without stepping up to Island Spas or Elite pricing. Pillowfall massagers and neck-and-shoulder jet systems are signature features.</p>
        <h2>Electrical: mostly 240V, with one plug-in option</h2>
        <p>Most South Seas models are 240V spas with a 5.5 kW heater. The 6-seat 840LE, for example, has a 5.0 BHP two-speed pump plus a 3.0 BHP pump and holds about 405 gallons. The exception is the <strong>519P</strong>: a 4-seat, 200-gallon spa that plugs into a 120V outlet with a 15-foot GFCI cord and uses a 1.4 kW heater. It's a good fit for patios and townhomes where adding a circuit isn't practical. Read <a href="/guides/110v-vs-240v-hot-tubs/">110V vs 240V</a> to decide which makes sense for you.</p>
        <h2>South Seas in a Utah winter</h2>
        <p>South Seas lists full foam as an optional feature. If you plan to soak all winter, ask us about it, along with a well-fitting <a href="/covers/">cover</a>. The 240V models' 5.5 kW heater recovers heat quickly on cold nights. See our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-utah-winter/">winter guide</a>.</p>
        <h2>See South Seas Spas in Midvale</h2>
        <p>We keep display models from every brand we carry at 6905 S State St in Midvale (Mon–Sat, 10 AM–5 PM). Floor models change, so <a href="/contact/">call or message us</a> if you want to sit in a specific model before you visit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

